# KEYMAP.md §Global (Normal mode, all Hub screens) — `i` toggles the detail panel,
# "never focusable; it mirrors the cursor row". UX-SPEC §3.4: the panel is open by default in a
# window at least 1120 px wide, which the harness's 1440 px window is.
#
# The panel's buttons are the oracle for whether it is drawn (`detail.open` is its primary
# button); the snapshot can otherwise only say what the panel must *not* change: the mode, the
# focused row and the selection are identical either side of the toggle, and moving the cursor
# with the panel open is still an ordinary list move. What the panel looks like is the
# screenshots' job.
fixture: busy
await idle 30000
assert screen == Hub && hub_pane == List && focused == worktrees.row[0]
assert lists.worktrees.selected.label == spike
assert targets["detail.open"] exists && targets["detail.menu"] exists
shot detail-open
dump detail-open

# The panel mirrors the cursor, so moving the cursor is still an ordinary list move.
key j
await focused == worktrees.row[1]
assert lists.worktrees.selected.label == broken && hub_pane == List
shot detail-broken

# `i` closes it without taking focus or changing the mode.
key i
await targets["detail.open"] absent
assert mode == Normal && hub_pane == List && focused == worktrees.row[1] && overlay absent
assert lists.worktrees.selected.label == broken
shot detail-closed
dump detail-closed

# `i` opens it again, and the cursor stays exactly where the panel left it.
key i
await targets["detail.open"] exists
assert mode == Normal && hub_pane == List && focused == worktrees.row[1] && overlay absent
quit
